WEBVTT

00:16:56.954 --> 00:17:00.304
could be generated
by the machinery of the brain.

00:17:00.804 --> 00:17:03.226
Now, 250 years later,

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:06.536
I think we're beginning
to glimpse how this is done.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:07.760
Thanks very much.

00:17:07.784 --> 00:17:10.761
(Applause)

00:17:10.785 --> 00:17:13.762
Chris Anderson: That was superb.
Thank you so much.

00:17:13.786 --> 00:17:16.756
You speak about these things
with so much insight

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:19.231
and empathy for your patients.

00:17:19.623 --> 00:17:23.443
Have you yourself experienced
any of the syndromes you write about?

00:17:23.467 --> 00:17:25.684
Oliver Sacks: I was afraid
you would ask that.

00:17:25.708 --> 00:17:27.536
(Laughter)

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.928
Well, yeah, a lot of them.

00:17:29.952 --> 00:17:33.019
And, actually, I'm a little
visually impaired myself.